            {"name": "Gross Long", "exposure_percent": 0.35, "grouped_metric_value": "Equity"},
            {"name": "Gross Long", "exposure_percent": 0.20, "grouped_metric_value": "Options"}
        ]
    }
]
```

Get LTD yearly performance breakdown with cumulative PnL as percentage of NAV.

Returns yearly breakdown plus overall LTD total for the specified date range.
Years are derived from the date_range.

## Example Request (minimal)

```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-20"
    }
}
```

## Example Request (with fund filter)

```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-20"
    },
    "filters": {
        "fund_name": ["Flagship"]
    }
}
```

Get historical performance monthly breakdown for all values of a selected dimension.

Consolidates N*(M+1) separate calls into a single request.
For each unique value of the selected dimension (group_by), runs overall +
monthly queries with that value as a filter, so PnL % NAV is scoped to each
value's own NAV.

Response is pivoted: one row per dimension value, months as columns.

## Example Request (by fund_name)

```json
{
    "year": 2026,
    "group_by": ["fund_name"],
    "filters": {}
}
```

## Example Response

```json
{
    "data": [
        {"fund_name": "Flagship", "Jan 2026": 0.02, "Feb 2026": 0.04, "PNL (% NAV)": 0.06},
        {"fund_name": "Innovation", "Jan 2026": 0.03, "Feb 2026": 0.05, "PNL (% NAV)": 0.08}
    ],
    "metadata": {...}
}
```

Get team analyst breakdown statistics with alpha analysis per benchmark.

Returns two data sections:
- data[0]: Primary analyst breakdown (grouped by primary_analyst)
- data[1]: Secondary analyst breakdown (grouped by secondary_analyst)

Each analyst row contains per-benchmark alpha columns, e.g.
"Alpha (vs DJSMDQT Index)" and "Alpha (vs XHE US Equity)".

Use `filters.portfolio_team` to filter by team (e.g., ["Medical Technology"] or ["Therapeutics"]).

## Example Request

```json
{
    "date_range": {"start_date": "2026-01-01", "end_date": "2026-02-20"},
    "filters": {"portfolio_team": ["Medical Technology"]},
    "benchmark_ids": ["DJSMDQT Index", "XHE US Equity"],
    "sort": {"sort_by": ["average_net_exposure"], "sort_descending": true}
}
```

## Example Response (abbreviated)

```json
{
    "data": [
        {
            "metadata": {"group_by": ["primary_analyst"], ...},
            "data": [
                {
                    "primary_analyst": "Alex Demo",
                    "primary_analyst_avatar": "alex@example.test|Alex|Demo",
                    "cumulative_pnl": -99641762.77,
                    "cumulative_pnl_percent_nav": -0.0118,
                    "cumulative_group_pnl_percent": -0.1539,
                    "Alpha (vs DJSMDQT Index)": -0.1102,
                    "Alpha (vs XHE US Equity)": -0.1463,
                    "average_net_exposure": 601182825.20
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "metadata": {"group_by": ["secondary_analyst"], ...},
            "data": [...]
        }
    ]
}
```

Get merged analyst metrics combining primary and secondary analyst PnL.

Merges primary and secondary analyst contributions using the formula:
    merged_pnl = primary_pnl + 0.5 * secondary_pnl

This provides a blended view of each analyst's total PnL contribution,
giving full credit for primary coverage and half credit for secondary coverage.

## Example Request

```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2026-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-20"
    },
    "filters": {},
    "sort": {
        "sort_by": ["cumulative_merged_pnl_percent_nav"],
        "sort_descending": true
    }
}
```

## Example Response

```json
{
    "data": [
        {
            "analyst_name": "John Doe",
            "analyst_avatar": "https://...",
            "cumulative_merged_pnl_percent_nav": 0.045,
            "primary_cumulative_pnl_percent_nav": 0.03,
            "secondary_cumulative_pnl_percent_nav": 0.03,
            "primary_average_net_exposure": 15000000,
            "secondary_average_net_exposure": 8000000
        }
    ],
    "metadata": {...}
}
```

Get LTD alpha yearly alpha performance statistics.

Calculates alpha metrics across yearly periods and the overall LTD range.
Response is pivoted with year labels as columns. Row identity depends on
``group_by``:

- ``group_by`` omitted/null (default): one row per benchmark.
- ``group_by=["primary_analyst"]``: one row per analyst within the filter
  scope (with avatar). Designed for single-benchmark dropdown UIs.

Routes between fund-level and non-fund-level alpha based on filters:
- Fund-level (filters only have fund_name or empty): uses `metric` field to select metric
  (default: cumulative_simple_alpha_pnl_percent_nav)
- Non-fund-level (filters have non-fund_name keys): uses cumulative_alpha_pnl_percent

## Example Request (non-fund-level)
```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-23"
    },
    "benchmark_ids": ["RGUSHSBT Index", "XBI US Equity", "NBI Index"],
    "filters": {
        "portfolio_team": ["Hedge"]
    }
}
```

## Example Request (fund-level, default metric)
```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-23"
    },
    "benchmark_ids": ["RGUSHSBT Index", "XBI US Equity", "NBI Index"],
    "filters": {
        "fund_name": ["Flagship"]
    }
}
```

## Example Request (fund-level, net-adjusted alpha)
```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-02-23"
    },
    "benchmark_ids": ["RGUSHSBT Index", "XBI US Equity", "NBI Index"],
    "filters": {
        "fund_name": ["Flagship"]
    },
    "metric": "cumulative_net_adjusted_alpha_pnl_percent_nav"
}
```

## Example Request (analyst-grouped, single benchmark)
```json
{
    "date_range": {
        "start_date": "2021-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-05-11"
    },
    "benchmark_ids": ["XHE US Equity"],
    "filters": {
        "portfolio_team": ["Medical Technology"]
    },
    "group_by": ["primary_analyst"]
}
```

## Example Response (benchmark-rowed)
```json
{
    "data": [
        {"benchmark_id": "RGUSHSBT Index", "2021": 2.563, "2022": 0.203, "LTD": 2.646},
        {"benchmark_id": "XBI US Equity", "2021": 2.478, "2022": 0.104, "LTD": 2.376},
        {"benchmark_id": "NBI Index", "2021": 2.319, "2022": 0.011, "LTD": 2.080}
    ],
    "metadata": {...}
}
```

## Example Response (analyst-rowed)
```json
{
    "data": [
        {"primary_analyst": "Alice", "primary_analyst_avatar": "alice@…|Alice|Doe",
         "2021": 0.012, "2022": 0.034, "ALPHA PNL (% NMV)": 0.087},
        {"primary_analyst": "N/C", "primary_analyst_avatar": "N/C",
         "2021": null, "2022": 0.001, "ALPHA PNL (% NMV)": 0.004}
    ],
    "metadata": {...}
}
```

400.description:
Bad request. One of:
- metrics array is empty; omit field for all metrics.
- Unknown metric(s): {names}
- STLY is not supported with ITD period.
- Unknown template(s): {names}

CompanyComparisonFilter.description:
A single comparison filter for filtering companies by field values.

This filter represents a single comparison operation between a company field
and a provided value using a specified operator. It's the basic building block
for creating filter expressions in the company API.

The filter supports standard fields and related entity fields (using dot notation),
with special handling for list fields. When the filter is applied, it's converted
to a Polars expression that can be efficiently executed against the company data.

Examples:
    - Simple text search: {"field": "name", "op": "contains", "value": "Bio"}
    - Numeric comparison: {"field": "market_cap", "op": "gt", "value": 1000000000}
    - Related field: {"field": "primary_instrument.ticker", "op": "eq", "value": "AAPL"}
    - Weighted attribute: {"field": "weighted_attributes.therapeutic_areas.value", "op": "contains", "value": "Oncology"}

CompanyLogicalFilter.description:
A logical filter that combines multiple company filters with boolean operations.

This filter allows for the creation of complex filter expressions by combining
multiple comparison filters or other logical filters using boolean operations
like AND, OR, and NOT. It enables sophisticated querying capabilities similar
to what's possible with SQL WHERE clauses.

Logical operators:
- and: All conditions must be true (default for multiple conditions)
- or: At least one condition must be true
- not: Negates the condition

Examples:
    AND operation (all conditions must match):
    ```json
    {
        "op": "and",
        "filters": [
            {"field": "market_cap", "op": "gte", "value": 1000000000},
            {"field": "name", "op": "contains", "value": "Tech"}
        ]
    }
    ```

    OR operation (any condition can match):
    ```json
    {
        "op": "or",
        "filters": [
            {"field": "name", "op": "contains", "value": "Health"},
            {"field": "name", "op": "contains", "value": "Bio"}
        ]
    }
    ```

    NOT operation (negates a condition):
    ```json
    {
        "op": "not",
        "filters": [
            {"field": "workflow_status", "op": "eq", "value": "flagged"}
        ]
    }
    ```

    Nested operations (for complex queries):
    ```json
    {
        "op": "and",
        "filters": [
            {"field": "market_cap", "op": "gte", "value": 1000000000},
            {
                "op": "or",
                "filters": [
                    {"field": "primary_analyst.name", "op": "contains", "value": "Smith"},
                    {"field": "secondary_analysts.name", "op": "contains", "value": "Jones"}
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
    ```

HistPerfMonthlyAlphaPerfResponse.description:
Response model for Historical Perf Monthly Alpha Perf metrics.

Data is pivoted: rows are dimension values, columns are months.

Example (non-fund, group_by=fund_name):
    {"data": [
        {"fund_name": "Flagship", "Jan 2025": 0.019, ..., "ALPHA PNL (% NMV)": 0.227},
        {"fund_name": "DemoBio", "Jan 2025": 0, ..., "ALPHA PNL (% NMV)": 0},
        {"fund_name": "Innovation", "Jan 2025": 0, ..., "ALPHA PNL (% NMV)": 0}
    ]}
